  "notes": "5S IN JAPANESE WORKPLACES:\n{整頓|せいとん} is one of the famous \"5S\" workplace organization principles:\n- {整理|せいり} (seiri) - sort\n- {整頓|せいとん} (seiton) - set in order\n- {清掃|せいそう} (seiso) - shine/clean\n- {清潔|せいけつ} (seiketsu) - standardize\n- {躾|しつけ} (shitsuke) - sustain\n\nCOMMON PAIR:\n{整理|せいり}{整頓|せいとん} is often used as a set phrase meaning \"organizing and tidying up.\"\n\nDIFFERENCE FROM {整理|せいり}:\n- {整理|せいり} - organizing, sorting (includes discarding unnecessary items)\n- {整頓|せいとん} - tidying, arranging (putting things in proper places)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {身|み}の{回|まわ}りの{整頓|せいとん} - organizing one's personal space\n- {整頓|せいとん}された{部屋|へや} - a tidy room",
